Upgrade procedure for file(1) / libmagic

Source: https://astron.com/pub/file/file-VERSION.tar.gz
        (see https://www.darwinsys.com/file/ for release announcements;
        check the .asc next to it, signed by Christos Zoulas,
        BE04995BA8F90ED0C0C176C471112AB16CB33B3A)

To upgrade to a new version:

1. Download, verify and extract the new tarball to /tmp/file/file-VERSION
2. Use the vendor-update skill (vendor/file/dist, contrib/file, tag
   vendor/file/dist/VERSION).  The vendor branch carries the full
   tarball; nothing is pruned.
3. Update lib/libmagic/config.h: bump PACKAGE_STRING, PACKAGE_VERSION
   and VERSION, and add any new macros from config.h.in.  FreeBSD's
   lib/libmagic/config.h is a good reference; the only intended
   difference is HAVE_BYTESWAP_H, which we probe with __has_include
   because mkmagic is built with the host's headers.
4. Check lib/libmagic/Makefile for new source files (SRCS and the
   mkmagic rule).  New magic/Magdir files are picked up by a glob.
5. Build lib/libmagic and usr.bin/file, and run the file tests
   (usr.bin/file/tests, which uses contrib/file/tests).

Local patches applied on top of upstream:

  None as of file 5.48.  The FreeBSD UFS2 flags patch (f0ca30b4e500)
  and the apprentice.c byte-swap fix (faa5141b9be4) are upstream now,
  and the old gpkg-1-zst.result tweak is no longer needed.

Notes:
  - Check FreeBSD's contrib/file/ git log for any new local patches
    after each upstream import.
  - If a result file in contrib/file/tests lacks a trailing newline,
    the test fails; FreeBSD normalizes them in
    usr.bin/file/tests/Makefile.  file 5.48 has none.
